From 4398de08166b3f2414300ea81d68177bae91d594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 04:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Space answers a ringing call on the in-call screen

For phones with a hardware keyboard (Q25): when a call rings and no
other call is active, on hold or dialling out, Space answers it as an
audio call, the same as the green CALL key.

* Behind Settings > Sounds and vibration > In-call > "Space answers
  calls" (sable_space_answers, device-protected preferences so it works
  before first unlock), on by default.
* Handled in dispatchKeyEvent, before the view hierarchy, so a focused
  Decline control never takes the press; the repeats and release of
  the press that answered are swallowed so they cannot reach the
  in-call controls that replace the answer screen.
* With call waiting the on-screen choice (hold or end the other call)
  decides; Space does nothing there.
* Space never hangs up. Ending a call is unchanged: the red key per
  platform policy (ENDCALL, or Power when "Power button ends call" is
  on) and the on-screen End button.
* Held keys and Space with Shift, Alt, Sym, Ctrl, Meta or Fn keep the
  upstream meaning.

The decision is SableInCallKeys.decideIncoming (pure); host tests live
in the SableOS Q25 repository under tests/framework/packages/apps/Dialer.
